ne with something that important. That's not offensive. That's sensible. So maybe the question isn't "does this person lack the ultimate accountability layer?" but "what does his actual track record say, and have I observed enough of it to feel safe?" If the answer is "not yet," then you have a perfectly good reason to say no—one that doesn't require bringing theology into it at all.
